Recursion:
in java, whena function calls a copy of itself then the process is known as Recursion

Syntax:
void recursion()
{
recursion();// the recursive function calls itself inside the same function
}
public static void main(String[] args){
recursion(); // function call
}

Types of Recursion
                    Recursion
                        |
           ----------------------------
           |                           |
           |                           |
        Direct                      Indirect
           |                           
         Tail
         Head
         Tree
        Nested
        Linear

Direct Recursion:
when a function calls itself within the same function repeatedly, it is called the direct recursion

Structure:
fun()
{
fun();
}

Indirect Recursion function:
when a function is mutually called by another function in a circular manner, the function is called an indirect recursion function.

Structure:
fun1()
{
fun2()
}
fun2()
{
fun3()
}

TAIL RECURSION    


        fun(3)
         |
   - - - - - - - -
   |             | 
print 3        fun(2)
                 |
        -------------------
        |                  |
      print 2            fun(1)
                           |
                   --- - - - - - - -
                  |                 |
            print 0               fun(0)    the condition becomes false

// TAIL Recursion
import java.util.*;
public class Main{
    static void fun(int n){
        if(n!=0){
            System.out.print(n + " ");
            fun(n-1);
        }
    }
public static void main(String[] args){
    Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
    int num = sc.nextInt();
    fun (num);
}
}
